Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA  History of invasive lobular carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  Right breast simple mastectomy  Has had chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR FLAP   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  LERWILL  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 13 43                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying tan irregular skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The inferior aspect of the skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nipple areolar complex which is unremarkable  The superior aspect of the skin ellipse contains a 2 0cm curvilinear  well healed scar  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan white cavitary lesion  with adjacent areas of focal hemorrhage  consistent with prior biopsy site  This area is located directly posterior to the previously described scar on the skin surface  The biopsy cavity comes to 0 1cm of the posterior margin and abuts the anterior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is predominantly fatty with only focal areas of fibrosis  One area of fibrosis in the lateral aspect of the breast contains a focal REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of tan brown discoloration  Distinct nodules or masses are not identified  Serial sectioning of the axillary region reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity to posterior margin  B  Biopsy cavity to anterior margin with a small amount of overlying skin  C D  Further sections of biopsy cavity  E  Sections of fibrosis away from biopsy cavity containing tan brown discoloration  F  Sections of fibrosis away from biopsy cavity with closest posterior margin  G  One axillary lymph node  bisected  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional anterior flap right breast  is an irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal homogenous  tan yellow lobulated tissue consistent with adipose tissue  No areas of fibrosis are identified  No nodules or masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted in H and I  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Mary Catherine Hertl  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR FLAP  EXCISION , No.
