Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 02 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 02 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA  42 year old female with history of invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma in the left breast  now with simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL STROMALLY INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA IS NOT SEEN  NOTE  One lymph node is replaced by tumor and measures 0 25cm in greatest dimension  Slight extranodal extension is present  The adjacent 0 3cm lymph node contains a 0 05cm metastatic deposit  These two lymph nodes are in the area denoted by the stitch  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  29 MAY 02 at 18 18                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  designated as  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE kilogram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy oriented by a bow tie designating the axillary end and a suture designating an  alleged tumor or lymph node   The anterior aspect of the specimen is notable for a REMOVED_DATE x 13 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm nipple and a 4 5cm well healed scar  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm cavity consistent with previous excisional biopsy  located beneath the scar and 0 2cm from the deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is composed of 80  adipose and 20  fibrous tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm firm area is identified in the area marked by the suture  Additional discrete nodules that are easily expressed from the tissue are identified between the stitch and the biopsy