Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 38 CLINICAL DATA  66 year old with history of right mastectomy for breast cancer  now with new suspicious left breast mass at 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSIES  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Note  Receptor studies will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  are 8 tan pink cores of tissue  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSIES , Not reported.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 28 CLINICAL DATA  An excisional biopsy on REMOVED_DATE showed invasive ductal carcinoma  grade III III with lymphatic invasion and free margins  There was also ductal carcinoma in situ extending to within 0 1cm of one margin  A re excision on REMOVED_DATE showed ductal carcinoma in situ grade III III extending to within 0 4cm of a margin  as well as extensive lymphatic permeation by carcinoma extending to within less than 0 1cm from a margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 41                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 1 006 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with an irregular contour  A REMOVED_DATE x 9 9cm skin ellipse is attached  with an areola which measures 5 8cm in diameter and a nipple which measures 1 3cm in diameter  There is a 4 9cm linear scar located 5 3cm lateral to the nipple  The overlying skin is otherwise externally unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  Externally  the specimen is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm biopsy cavity which is open and in communication with the deep  posterior  margin  The specimen is inked as follows  black intact deep  posterior  margin  blue superior lateral quadrant  orange  superior medial quadrant  green inferior lateral quadrant  yellow inferior medial quadrant  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal that the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm biopsy cavity extends to within 2 5cm of the anterior margin in the superior lateral quadrant and underlies the linear scar noted on the skin ellipse  Radiating in all directions from the biopsy cavity is irregular  firm  white yellow scar tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow  fibrofatty and unremarkable  It is extensively searched for lymph nodes  and none is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Biopsy cavity to adjacent deep margin  C F  Biopsy cavity  G  Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity in superior lateral quadrant  H   Lymph node  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , No.
