Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Evan Farkash  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ  status post excision with positive margins  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADJACENT TO HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND  0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL  575   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a mastectomy specimen that has been previously oriented by the surgeon with a stitch designating the axillary tail  The specimen measures 23cm from medial to lateral  23 5cm from inferior to superior  and 5 4cm from anterior to posterior  The specimen is surfaced by a skin ellipse measuring 20 2cm x 11 3cm  There is an areolar region measuring 2 9cm in greatest diameter and a nipple which is not retracted measuring 1 1cm in greatest diameter  The specimen is notable for a single well healed scar measuring 3 5cm in length and located 6 5cm from the areolar region at the 3 o clock position  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal white fibrous and yellow fatty parenchyma with a firm white and red region consistent with previous biopsy site underlying the scar on the skin ellipse  The biopsy cavity measures 2 5cm medial to lateral  1 8cm anterior to posterior and 2 4cm superior to inferior  The biopsy cavity is located 1 5cm from the posterior deep margin and 3 5cm from the anterior margin of resection  Lymph nodes are not identified along the axillary aspect  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity in region with sentinel lymph node dye  Received in formalin  labeled  left axilla sentinel node  575   is a portion of yellow tan fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  containing potential lymph node  The specimen is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  report_end  , Not reported.
