bmitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nodule with closest resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the central aspect of the specimen  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen  which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm portion of wrinkled tan skin with an unremarkable nipple areolar complex with a centrally located 1 1cm in diameter nipple  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a stitch designating the 6 o clock position  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal 3 tan pink  well circumscribed nodules within the lower outer quadrant  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  3cm from the closest posterior margin   REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  2cm from the closest posterior margin   and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  2 4cm from the closest inferior margin   The remaining breast parenchyma consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified within the axillary tail of the specimen  Also received within the same container is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of irregular portions of tan yellow unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the largest nodule to nearest anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the mid sized nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the smallest nodule   R