st   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left radical modified mastectomy specimen with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan brown skin ellipse which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 6 5cm linear well healed scar present in the upper outer quadrant approximately between 2 00 and 3 o clock 4cm from the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm stellate fibrous area approximately beneath the linear well healed scar on the overlying skin in the upper outer quadrant  4 0cm from overlying anterior inked margin  and 2 4cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the stellate fibrous area contains foci of chalky discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  and a metallic clip  There are two tan brown  soft to firm  fairly well circumscribed cystic nodules present approximately 4 0cm and 8 0cm medial to the stellate fibrous area in the central and inner quadrant  The first REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan brown cyst in the central quadrant is present 4 0cm from the overlying anterior and 2 3cm from posterior inked margin  The second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan brown cyst in the inner quadrant is present 4 0cm from overlying anterior and 1 8cm from posterior inked margin  The remaining breast parenchyma contains tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with abundant amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  Multiple lymph noes dissected ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to 2 x 2 x 0 8cm Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  nodular fibrous breast parenchyma adjacent to the scar  outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire tan brown nodule  central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second tan brown nodule  inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma intervening of the two tan brown nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single trisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible lymph nodes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections breast parenchyma adjacent to scar in upper outer quadrant and surrounding tissue  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Left   Modified Radical Mastectomy  report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 35 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS close to edge single sutures  long   lateral  short   superior  double suture   most posterior margin side away from tumor bed                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 26 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The posterior surface is marked by a double stitch  lateral surface is marked by a long stitch  the superior surface is marked by a short stitch  The posterior surface consists of fibroadipose tissue and is grossly unremarkable  The anterior surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE white fibrinous area that extends to the lateral margin  a rubbery REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow well circumscribed nodule that extends to the medial border  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan yellow nodule that extends to within 0 3cm of the lateral superior border  On the anterior surface there are also several focal greenish gray regions ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm the remainder of the anterior surface has focal areas of hemorrhage  The posterior surface is inked in black  the anterior surface is inked in blue  and the superior posterior surface is overinked in yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal  The medial nodule has a yellow cut surface with areas of apparent fatty necrosis  superior lateral nodule has a yellow white cut surface with focal areas of hemorrhage  the fibrinous biopsy cavity has a yellow white cut surface the remainder of the parenchyma has a yellow white cut surface and is grossly unremarkable  Section code  A  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity nearest to the margin at the inferior aspect of the specimen  B  Representative sections of the medial nodule  C  Representative sections of the superior lateral nodule  D  Representative section of the biopsy cavity near the superior margin  E  Representative section of the parenchyma at the superior margin  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , No.
